rem Prime Factor and Exponent
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=779

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Depth integer = 1000
arg Reach integer = 4000000

rem Smallest prime p with p^a exactly
rem dividing n has density
rem D(p) (1 - 1/p) / p^a, where D(p) is
rem the product of 1 - 1/q over q < p.
rem With x = 1 / p the sum over a of
rem (a - 1) x^a is x^2 / (1 - x)^2, and
rem K = 1..Depth gives x (1 - x^Depth) /
rem (1 - x), so each prime adds
rem D(p) x^3 (1 - x^Depth) / (1 - x)^2.
Primes = primes to Reach copy
Inv = 1.0 / Primes
Before = (1.0 - Inv) scan * with 1.0
Dens = Before take (Primes len)
Rate = Inv ** Depth
Tail = Inv * Inv * Inv * (1.0 - Rate)
Gap = (1.0 - Inv) * (1.0 - Inv)
Terms = Dens * Tail / Gap
Total = Terms sum
Answer = Total round 12
Answer print
